.TH SYNAPSE 1 "2026" "synapseids" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
synapse \- SynapseIDS administrative CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B synapse
[\fB\-\-server\fR \fIurl\fR]
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B synapse
is a thin client for a running
.BR synapsed .
It holds no analysis logic of its own; every command is an HTTP request to the
daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print daemon status as JSON.
.TP
.B models
List the loaded inference models.
.TP
.BI "flows " "[\-\-limit N]"
Print recent flow records.
.TP
.BI "classifications " "[\-\-limit N]"
Print recent classifications as a compact rolling\-log table.
.TP
.BI "replay " "file.pcap [\-\-speed S]"
Start a PCAP replay on the daemon.
.I S
is one of
.BR 0.5 ", " 1 ", " 2 ", " 10 " or " max .
.TP
.B replay-stop
Stop the running replay.
.TP
.B version
Print CLI build metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-server " url"
Base URL of the daemon. Defaults to
.B $SYNAPSE_SERVER
or
.BR http://127.0.0.1:8080 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
success;
.B 1
request failed;
.B 2
usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR synapsed (1)
.SH AUTHOR
kawaiipantsu / THUGS. Source at https://github.com/kawaiipantsu/synapseids
